(* Expression -- Hate Speech -- UWM Post v. U Of Wisconsin)S
0 -1056 M
0 -1072 M
0 -10 R
(The full text of UWM POST v. U. of Wisconsin. This recent district)S
0 -1088 M
0 -10 R
(court ruling goes into detail about the difference between protected)S
0 -1104 M
0 -10 R
(offensive expression and illegal harassment. It even mentions email.)S
0 -1120 M
0 -1136 M
0 -10 R
(It concludes: "The founding fathers of this nation produced a)S
0 -1152 M
0 -10 R
(remarkable document in the Constitution but it was ratified only with)S
0 -1168 M
0 -10 R
(the promise of the Bill of Rights.  The First Amendment is central to)S
0 -1184 M
0 -10 R
(our concept of freedom.  The God-given "unalienable rights" that the)S
0 -1200 M
0 -10 R
(infant nation rallied to in the Declaration of Independence can be)S
0 -1216 M
0 -10 R
(preserved only if their application is rigorously analyzed.)S
0 -1232 M
0 -1248 M
0 -10 R
(The problems of bigotry and discrimination sought to be addressed here)S
0 -1264 M
0 -10 R
(are real and truly corrosive of the educational environment.  But)S
0 -1280 M
0 -10 R
(freedom of speech is almost absolute in our land and the only)S
0 -1296 M
0 -10 R
(restriction the fighting words doctrine can abide is that based on the)S
0 -1312 M
0 -10 R
(fear of violent reaction.  Content-based prohibitions such as that in)S
0 -1328 M
0 -10 R
(the UW Rule, however well intended, simply cannot survive the)S
0 -1344 M
0 -10 R
(screening which our Constitution demands.")S
